  "name": "dotnet-mcp-builder",
  "description": "Build Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers in C#/.NET against the current ModelContextProtocol 1.x NuGet packages. Especially helps with cases the model often gets wrong without guidance — stale preview versions (it tends to pick 0.3 or 0.4 preview), MCP Apps (interactive UI rendered in the host), elicitation URL mode, per-session HTTP wiring, OAuth and reverse-proxy deploy specifics, and debugging concrete MapMcp / STDIO / Streamable-HTTP errors. Also covers the routine work — STDIO and Streamable HTTP transports (SSE is deprecated), tools, prompts, resources, sampling, roots, completions, logging — and a basic .NET MCP client. Trigger when the user says or implies any .NET MCP server work: ModelContextProtocol, McpServerTool, MapMcp, WithStdioServerTransport, \"MCP server in C#\", \"MCP tool in dotnet\", \"expose this as MCP\", or names a primitive (prompt/resource/elicitation/MCP App) in a .NET context. Skip for MCP work in other languages. Use when you need help with dotnet mcp builder.",
